A||||3||Richard Parnell||Somebody? Rear wheel well, pretty please.||||9||
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||12-04-1999||02:34 PM||||Does anyone know of a kit or method to make a flare for the rear wheelwell of a Fiero? I would like to make the wheelwell opening look smaller and have a slight flare like the front wheel wells of my 87 SC. Also that way I could put much wider tires on the back. But mostly it's to get the look of the rear well to not be so large. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Sage||12-04-1999||03:55 PM||||Richard:  You can use fiberglass to make a "one of" part on any car.  The Fiero lends itself well to this, if you stick with the panels that are fiberglass.  It would not work very well if you try to do it on any of the abs panels.  The proper way to do it would be to make a "plug"(full scale mock-up) of whatever it is you want to produce. Then make a mold and take your part out of that.  I have been looking for ideas for something to produce this way for the Fiero.  Anybody think there would be a market for these flares?  Doing it this way,(plug-mold-part) is time consuming, expensive and labor intensive, but it yields a very strong, long lasting good looking part.  Thoughts, comments, suggestions, insults?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-04-1999||09:46 PM||||Richard... I don't know if this is something that you'd be interested in, but IRM sells flared body panels for the Fiero. Similar to the IMSA race car. Look good, but are a bit expensive. I think FOCOA carries them, as well, but I've never dealt with them.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||12-04-1999||10:57 PM||||IRM sells an entire kit for $3500 that includes the rear flared fenders, but I don't know if they sell just the flares individually.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quick2.JPG" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quick2.JPG</A> ||||reg||1
